### Sea-level muon spectrum before and after a lead slab of leadT cm, with nothing else around:
### the EXPACS muons of the thick-lead scan (from 9.25 MeV, mu+ and mu-, Guan zenith shape,
### zenith < 75 deg) fall from a 2 x 2 m plane lying 0.1 mm above an 8 x 8 m lead slab in vacuum.
### Every muon enters the slab; one that gets through leaves it from below and keeps its energy to
### the end of the world (vacuum), so ekin is its kinetic energy before the lead and end_ke after.
### The slab is wide enough that no muon leaves it through a side. One process per thickness (or
### several, with different seeds), started by
###   sh scripts/lead_filter.sh [--below E] [--parts n] [jobs] [muons] [thicknesses in cm]
### which sets the aliases leadT (cm), leadFilterEvents, leadFilterSeed, leadFilterEmax (GeV, the
### top of the simulated spectrum: 108.118, or only what can leave the lead below E),
### leadFilterDir and leadFilterFile.

/tof/det/stations false
/tof/det/frame false
/tof/det/stack false
/tof/det/absorber false
/tof/det/leadWalls false
/tof/target/enable false
/tof/det/camera false
/tof/det/worldMaterial G4_Galactic
/tof/det/worldSize 1000 1000 300 cm
/tof/blocks/add PbSlab G4_Pb 0 0 0 800 800 {leadT} cm
/update

/control/divide leadFilterHalf {leadT} 2
/control/add leadFilterPlaneZ {leadFilterHalf} 0.01
/gun/seed {leadFilterSeed}
/OutputFormat 1
/EventFilter 0
/OutputDirectory {leadFilterDir}
/OutputFile {leadFilterFile}
/GeneralParticleSource 2
/tof/cosmic/model expacs
/tof/cosmic/species mu+ mu-
/tof/cosmic/angular all 2 mu+ guan mu- guan
/tof/cosmic/planeCenter 0 0 {leadFilterPlaneZ} cm
/tof/cosmic/halfX 100 cm
/tof/cosmic/halfY 100 cm
/tof/cosmic/thetaMax 75 deg
/tof/cosmic/monoEnergy 0 GeV
/tof/cosmic/energyMin 0.00924915 GeV
/tof/cosmic/energyMax {leadFilterEmax} GeV
/run/beamOn {leadFilterEvents}
